  "body": "## Goal\n\nQualify a guarded setup for a 10 mm steel plate, an explicitly specified internal start diameter and a left-compensated opening. Exercise a 3 mm start and 0.25 mm Berco wire on an independent synthetic profile. Verify the offered process identity on the installed control.\n\n#2954 extends an existing punch technology and separation setting to additional heights. This request also changes the threading diameter and opening setup. An installed quality name alone does not prove effective settings. See #2984.\n\n## Acceptance\n\nPass the actual height and drilled diameter to the complete native setup. Check the piece, work, thread position, named process identity, nominal contour and zero assigned steps on the offline Classic Cut 2S control. Repeat the import with a preexisting quality name.\n\nPreserve an explicit request for zero separation only when the workflow verifies the slug restraint and the control retains that setting. A test that exercises import alone must identify that limit. Distinguish a saved process request from verified effective process values. Do not enable erosion, infer a holding method or substitute a quality from a different height.\n\nUse measured pass clearance before advertising any qualified cutting process. Preserve atomic refusal for unsupported combinations. #3178 covers the selected reentrant opening geometry.\n\nSuggested labels: enhancement, P6, effort:high, area:post, source:agent.\n",
